From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:54:24 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 52/67] Plutonium: dmabufs for PipeWire consumers that import
 them

EXO-CAPTURE: Ash's PipeWire nodes offer XRGB/ARGB8888 dmabufs with the
linear modifier first (a mandatory modifier property, so only consumers
that import dmabufs take them), then shared memory as before. With a
dmabuf format, buffers are GBM buffers on the first render node (one
device per stream), their fds exported to the consumer, and each frame is
written through the buffer's mapping. Without a render node the stream is
shared memory only.
